- For example with a default COP Network, if Uniform Scale is 500, the XZ dimensions range from -500 to 500 each. (11 October 2026)
- You can access the individual components with @P.x and @P.z. (11 October 2026)
- Let's take a look at a script. (11 October 2026)
- {{{ #!vex if (@P.x > 0 && @P.z < 0) { @mask = 1; } }}} (11 October 2026)
- Section: Circle mask (11 October 2026)
- Circles are certainly one of the most often required shapes for masking. (11 October 2026)
- {{{ #!vex vector position = chv("position"); vector offset = set(position.x, 0, position.z); (11 October 2026)
- if (length(v@P - offset) < chf("radius" { @mask = chf("mask_strength"); } }}} (11 October 2026)
- The first line reads the values from a custom position vector. (11 October 2026)
- Section: Ring mask (11 October 2026)
- Instead of a circle, you can create a ring by defining a custom inner and outer radius. (11 October 2026)
- {{{ #!vex vector position = chv("position"); vector offset = set(position.x, 0, position.z); float midpoint = length(v@P - offset); (11 October 2026)
- if (midpoint > chf("inner_radius") && midpoint < chf("outer_radius" { @mask = chf("mask_strength"); } }}} (11 October 2026)
- The code is very similar to the script from the Circle mask chapter. (11 October 2026)
- Section: Oval mask (11 October 2026)
- Instead of a circle you can also create an oval mask. (11 October 2026)
- {{{ #!vex float a = chf("x_dimension"); float b = chf("z_dimension"); vector offset = chv("offset"); float rotation = radians(chf("rotation"; // Degree -> radians float mask_strength = chf("mask_strength"); // > ... (11 October 2026)
- // Position of the current pixel relative to its offset vector pos = set(@P.x - offset.x, @P.z - offset.z); (11 October 2026)
- // Rotate the ellipse vector rotated_pos; rotated_pos.x = cos(rotation) * pos.x - sin(rotation) * pos.y; rotated_pos.y = sin(rotation) * pos.x + cos(rotation) * pos.y; (11 October 2026)
- // Test ellipse equation with transformed coordinates float ellipse_equation = pow(rotated_pos.x / a, 2) + pow(rotated_pos.y / b, 2); (11 October 2026)
- if (ellipse_equation <= 1.0) { @mask = mask_strength; } }}} (11 October 2026)
- The first five lines define the parameters for customizing the ellipse. (11 October 2026)
- The script calculates a position vector with the offset. (11 October 2026)
